From 272945a58180718ff86b28d1550bef3fb3e10ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:59:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 119/119] dynarmic A64: dead flags at a block's exit
 (look-ahead), conditional branches on a compare's values

As A32's elide_dead_nzcv: a block reads the A64 code its successors start with (along their
branches, 64 instructions at most); when every path sets the flags before reading them, the
block doesn't store the flags its last setters make, and a B.cond at its end branches on a
cmp/cmn/test of the values they came from (CondFlagsSub64/Add64/Test64/NZ64, and A32's 32-bit
and float forms). With elide_dead_nzcv_abi, calls and returns end a path with the flags dead,
and a block ending in BL, BLR or RET has them dead at its exit. The code read is added to the
block's ranges (invalidation, the persistent cache's hash). Eden's 64-bit cores enable both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
